        1 Introduction

        AOS/VS is available as Model 3900 and also as Model 31133.  This
        release notice contains information about AOS/VS Model 3900. If you
        have a system with "Pre-Installed  AOS/VS", you should read the
        release notice for AOS/VS Model 31133 (085-000780-10). New machines
        that come with Pre-Installed AOS/VS are the  DS/7500; and ECLIPSE
        MV/5500 DC, MV/5600 DC, MV/3600 DC, MV/3500 DC, MV/3200 DC,MV/2500
        DC, MV/2000 DC, MV/1400 DC, and  MV/1000 DC computers. For all
        other machines, read this notice.

        This release notice contains information consistent with AOS/VS
        (Model 3900) 7.73 software. Revision 7.73 contains enhancements and
        changes to Release 7.72. This release notice should be read in
        conjuction with the AOS/VS 7.72 Update Notice, part number
        078-000105-30.

        If  you  are  running AOS/VS Model 31133 or 31446, read this
        release notice if you want to know about enhancements, changes  and
        other detailed  technical  information  not documented in the Model
        31133 release notice.  You may also want to read this notice if you
        have disabled  pre-installed  AOS/VS,  as explained in Appendix D
        of the manual  "Using  the  AOS/VS  System  Management Interface
        (SMI)" (069-000203-02).   The  Introduction,  Software,
        Installation, and Enhancement chapters are the  only  chapters with
        3900  or  31133 specific information.

        The  purpose  of this release notice is to provide you with
        information about Revision 7.73 of AOS/VS that is  not available in
        the AOS/VS documentation.

        This  release notice  provides  a compilation of the update notices
        produced for AOS/VS Revs. 7.72, as well as new information relative
        to  AOS/VS  Rev.  7.73.  Enhancements, changes, notes, and warnings
        newly introduced with AOS/VS Rev. 7.73 are  clearly  marked.   When
        referencing  other  items,  the  reader should assume that any item
        discussing  a  change  of  some  type,  introduced  in  an  earlier
        revision, also applies to revisions that followed it.  For example,
        an enhancement introduced in Rev 7.72 applies to Rev 7.73.

