        4 Enhancements and Changes

        4.1 Enhancements

        4.1.1  AGENT

               AGENT will follow the ANSI standard for labeling magnetic
               tapes. An ASCII ZERO will be stored before the creation and
               expiration date in the year 2000 and beyond. Otherwise, a
               space will be stored for the date till the year 1999. For
               example, the date Jan-22-2002 will be stored in the tape as
               "002022".  Here the ZERO in the first location specifies
               that the date is in the year 2000.  The date Jan-22-1998
               will be stored as " 98022".  Here the space specifies that
               the date is not in year 2000.

               Agent will validate the expiry period correctly, and will
               not overwrite the labeled media before its actual expiry
               period.

        4.1.2  AOSVS

               Date will be displayed properly in the year 2000 and beyond.

        4.1.3  CLI16

               CLI16 displays and accepts year in 2 digit. Year less than
               68 is considered as year between 2000 and 2067. For example,
               year 67 will be taken as year 2067. 
        AOS/VS Release Notice Rev. 7.73                              Page 9
               
        4.1.4  CLI32

               CLI32 now accepts date in 2-digit or 4-digit format. For
               example, to see the files which are created after January
               2000, you can either give the command
               FILESTATUS/after/date=1-jan-2000 or
               FILESTATUS/after/date=1-jan-00.

               CLI32 now displays or returns date as output in 2 digit or 4
               digit year format. The new CLI32 mode variable YEAR4DIGIT
               allows to select the 4 digit year display. Enter the command
               "YEAR4DIGIT ON" to see 4 digit year and the command
               "YEAR4DIGIT OFF" to see 2 digit year. The default mode is
               the 2 digit year format. The command "YEAR4DIGIT" with no
               arguments displays current mode.

        4.1.5  CONTEST

               Date will be displayed properly in the year 2000 and beyond.

        4.1.6  DISCO

               DISCO will now accept /START and /STOP switches, which were
               not functioning earlier. If the user gives year as >= 00 & <
               68, then it will be treated as the year between 2000 and
               2067. User is expected to give the date in proper format,
               else the switch will not function properly.

               Date will be displayed properly in the four digit format.

        4.1.7  DUMP_II/LOAD_II

               DUMP_II now writes label as per the ANSI standards. An ASCII
               ZERO will be stored before the creation and expiration date
               in the year 2000 and beyond. Otherwise, a space will be
               stored for the date till the year 1999.

               DUMP_II/LOAD_II will display year in 2 digit format. For
               example, the year will be displayed as "00" for the year
               2000.

               DUMP_II will validate the expiry period, and will not
               overwrite the Labeled volumes before its actual expiry
               period.

        4.1.8  EXEC

               FCU.PR will print the year in two digits in the header
               message.  It will print 00 for year 2000, 10 for the year
               2010 and so on. 
        AOS/VS Release Notice Rev. 7.73                             Page 10

               XLPT.PR will create a dump file with two digit year format
               in its name. For example, it will create memory dump file
               with name 03_nov_09.1_34_02.7.mdm on 3rd November 2009. 

        4.1.9  HISTOREPORT

               Date will be displayed properly in the year 2000 and beyond.

        4.1.10 LFE

               Date will be displayed properly in the year 2000 and beyond.

        4.1.11 MASM

               MASM will correctly display the year, in the timestamp of
               compilation for the year 2000 and beyond. It will display 00
               for the year 2000, 10 for year 2010 and so on.

        4.1.12 MSCOPY

               MSCOPY will follow the ANSI standard for labeling labeled
               magnetic tapes. An ASCII ZERO will be stored before the
               creation and expiration date in the year 2000 and beyond.
               Otherwise, a space will be stored for the date till the year
               1999. For example, the date Jan-22-2002 will be stored in
               the tape as "002022".  Here the ZERO in the first location
               specifies that the date is in the year 2000.  The date
               Jan-22-1998 will be stored as " 98022".  Here the space
               specifies that the date is not in year 2000.

               MSCOPY  will  validate  the expiry  period correctly, and
               will not overwrite the labeled media before its actual
               expiry period.

        4.1.13 PCOPY

               PCOPY will accept and display year in two digit. Year less
               than 68 will be taken as year between 2000 and 2067. So year
               2000 will be displayed as "00" and year 67 will be taken as
               year 2067.

               PCOPY will write creation and expiry dates on labeled tapes
               as per ANSI standard. An ASCII ZERO will be stored if date
               is in the year 2000 and beyond. Otherwise, a SPACE is stored
               till 1999. 

               PCOPY will do a proper validation and will not overwrite the
               labeled tapes before their actual expiry period.

        4.1.14 PREDITOR

               Date will be displayed properly in the year 2000 and beyond.
               
        AOS/VS Release Notice Rev. 7.73                             Page 11

        4.1.15 REPORT

               REPORT accepts /AFTER and /BEFORE switches. If the user
               gives year as >= 00 & < 68, then it will treated as the year
               between 2000 and 2067.

        4.1.16 STARTER

               Date will be displayed properly in the year 2000 and beyond.

               Starter will accept the year >= 00 & < 68 for setting the
               date in the year between 2000 and 2067. For example, the
               date 01-Jan-00 will be treated as 01-Jan-2000.

        4.1.17 Terminal Services

               Termserver panic breakfile is created in :TSDUMPS directory
               as TS.devicecode.DDMMMYY.HHMMSS. The file will be created in
               proper format in the year 2000 and beyond.  Year will be
               returned in two digit. For example, 00 in 2000 and 10 in
               2010.


